{
  "rationale": "The model separates sensing from motion capability and uses small deterministic specifications to map each sensed condition to exactly one safe action. Clear conditions strongly favor forward progress, with a brief random-walk diversification layer to avoid excessively long straight runs. Obstacle states always pass through dedicated recovery states, use backward motion only for front-obstacle escape, prefer directed turns for side obstacles, and return to forward exploration immediately on path_clear. Commit/recovery states are one-shot and keep path_clear self-looped so open-loop pulses are not unnecessarily preempted.",
  "strategy": [
    "Use one plant for local perception outcomes and one plant for available motion commands",
    "Use specification automata to bind clear sensing to forward/random exploration and obstacle sensing to dedicated recovery actions",
    "Add a small alternation specification so clear-space behavior is mostly forward but occasionally random_walk",
    "Keep obstacle recovery conservative and one-shot, with immediate return to exploration when path_clear is observed"
  ],
